Subject: [PATCH 05/18] nemotron: Super's MTP head drafts over the embedded
 draft vocabulary's FP8 output rows

The draft head was the target's own, so every chain level read the whole FP8 output head. It now packs the
checkpoint's FP8 lm_head rows for the embedded draft vocabulary into a lane weight of their own and uploads their
vocabulary ids; a level proposes over that subset and the target still verifies every proposal with its full head, so
replies are unchanged. A level falls from 3.55 to 2.16 ms on a GB10, for 192 MiB beside the full head.
